  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:harav_et_riveinu">
        <tei:p><tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en">After the reading of the Megillah, if there is a minyan of ten adult males present, the following is recited.</tei:note><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/1"/>Blessed are You, Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/2"/>our God, King of the universe,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/3"/>Who defends our cause,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/4"/>judges our grievances,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/5"/>takes vengeance for us,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/6"/>brings retribution
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/7"/>upon all our mortal enemies
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/8"/>and exacts payment [punishment]
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/9"/>from our oppressors.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/10"/>Blessed are You, Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/11"/>Who exacts payment [punishment]
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/12"/>in behalf of His people, Israel
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/13"/>from all their oppressors,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/14"/>the Almighty, the Deliverer.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/15"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/16"/>The rose of Jacob cheered and rejoiced<tei:anchor xml:id="note_1"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/17"/>when they [all] saw
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/18"/>Mordechai dressed in royal blue.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/19"/>You have always been their deliverance,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/20"/>their hope in every generation,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/21"/>to make known
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/22"/>that all who hope in You
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/23"/>will never be shamed,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/24"/>and never will be disgraced
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:harav_et_riveinu/25"/>those who trust in You.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
  <tei:standOff type="notes">
    <tei:note type="commentary" target="#note_1" xml:lang="en">
      <tei:p>The opening sentence refers to the city of Shushan and paraphrases the verse, “And the city of Shushan cheered and rejoiced” Esther 8:15.</tei:p>
    </tei:note>
  </tei:standOff>
